# Capture replay truth (#317)

Following ADR 012 and architecture/historical-replay.md, capture selection is
successful only after the player has read usable recorded prints or quotes.
Missing, unreadable, malformed-only, empty and L2/bar-only sessions are refused.
Failed selection clears capture identity and returns replay_source=synthetic,
replay_ok=false and replay_error; the error persists in clock polls until an
explicit successful selection or Close replay. The header renders the error
and never opens the rejected ticker. After a failed attempt the feed emits nothing until an explicit successful
selection or Close replay, preventing a silent fabricated fallback.

Session listings retain empty recordings for diagnosis, with empty, usable and
unavailable_reason fields. Byte presence is a cheap availability hint, not proof
of valid rows; the loader remains authoritative. Disabled sessions cannot be
picked. Valid quotes-only captures remain usable.

The capture feed publishes only recorded prints on the recorded symbol. Quiet
intervals may refresh an actual captured book, but never manufacture GAP prints,
zero prices, or invented quotes or depth. Capture feed failure stops that tick
and reports replay failure instead of falling through to the synthetic generator.
A synthetic tick is permitted only when synthetic playback is explicitly active.

Parsing and availability helpers belong to the capture domain, and capture feed
fan-out belongs to the SIM feature (ADR 001 module ownership). Keep existing
fidelity and L2 decimation policy unchanged in this fix.
